DEVICE VERIFICATION, AND ITS LIMITS

crDroid 17.0 edition, 2026-10-20: strict apply and reverse at the reference commits in this NOTICE.
Device-verified on a OnePlus 13 on 2026-10-20 (both threshold modes, pause at the limit,
restore on game exit); also built into the maintainer's crDroid 17.0 ROM of 2026-10-22
(repository commit 4bdecab). The crDroid 16.0
edition is kept on branch 16.0 of this repository.

Verified on a OnePlus 13 running crDroid 16.0, in eight charge-pause
cycles across four games, plus a reboot while a game was in the foreground:

  threshold 70 %            engaged and applied, eight cycles
  charge stop at threshold  battery status 2 (charging) -> 4 (not charging),
                            current -2976 mA -> 0 mA at exactly level 70
  restore on game exit      eight cycles, always to the stored original state
  restore after reboot      stored state replayed and cleared 82 s after boot
  rapid game switching      stable down to 0.5 s between cycles
  no game running           charging is never touched

The thresholds 80, 90 and 100 % were NOT verified on a device. That the
LineageOS provider accepts them was measured separately (values below 70 are
rejected by its validator), which is not the same as a device test of the
GameSpace path.

The "battery level at game start" option raises a start level below 70 to 70,
because the LineageOS validator rejects anything lower. This was verified on the
device at 69 % battery: the log reports the threshold as 70, not 69.
